course: dictionary
lesson: 1628
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word chi is one example. When you meet it, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Tai chi is a slow exercise from China.» The words exercise and China are the clues. Chi here is part of a named exercise, not a letter or a food.
explain: «The chi-squared test» is used in statistics, which is maths about numbers and data. The word chi here is a Greek letter. Chī, said "chir", is a different word again: «chī fàn le ma?» uses chī, which means "to eat".
fact: Chi is the 22nd letter of the Greek alphabet. It is written χ and said "kye", rhyming with "sky".
fact: Chi can also be spelled qi. In Chinese belief, it is a life energy said to flow through the body and nature.
fact: Chī is a Mandarin word meaning "to eat", as in chī fàn, "eat a meal". It is not an English word.
fact: «Tai chi» is a slow exercise from China, and it is one of the main uses of the word chi in English.
fact: «Mischievous» is spelled M-I-S-C-H-I-E-V-O-U-S and said "MIS-chi-vus"; «mischievious», with an extra "i", is a very common mistake.
exercise: In «chī fàn le ma?», what does chī mean? | to sleep | *to eat | to read | to walk
exercise: In «Tai chi is a slow exercise from China», what is tai chi? | a Greek letter | a number in maths | *a slow exercise from China | a type of food
exercise: «Mischievous» is spelled M-I-S-C-H-I-E-V-O-U-S. Which spelling is correct? | mischivous | mischievious | *mischievous | mischevious
test: In statistics, the Greek letter χ appears in which test? | *chi-squared test | a bowl of rice | tai chi class | chī fàn
test: Qi, also spelled chi, is what, in Chinese belief? | a type of statistics | a Greek letter | the word for to eat | *a life energy said to flow through the body
exam: A friend asks «chī fàn le ma?». What is the friend asking? | *Have you eaten? | Did you sleep well? | Where is the library? | Do you like tai chi?
